# mytheus-platform / env/prod.db.relay.env - the OUTBOX RELAY database credential.
# Copy to env/prod.db.relay.env and fill. NEVER commit the filled file.
#
# Layered on top of env/prod.env by the `relay` service only.
#
# `mytheus_relay` holds SELECT and UPDATE on `outbox` and no grant on any other table. Its
# single permissive `outbox_relay_drain` policy is what lets it read every tenant's rows
# without BYPASSRLS, which keeps the cross-tenant reach visible in `pg_policies` instead of
# hidden in a role attribute.
#
# Both variables are set to the relay role deliberately. `RELAY_DATABASE_URL` is what
# services/relay/main.py reads; `DATABASE_URL` is the fallback, and pointing the fallback at
# `mytheus_app` would mean the relay silently drains nothing (defect D4).
RELAY_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://mytheus_relay:CHANGE_ME_relay_password@postgres:5432/mytheus
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://mytheus_relay:CHANGE_ME_relay_password@postgres:5432/mytheus
